ard Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Nancy Mace (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Nancy Mace's retirement leaves this Lowcountry seat open, returning it to its underlying Republican lean of about six points. Jenny Costa Honeycutt, the Republican nominee, faces Democrat Nancy Lacore, a self-funded contender who has raised more than four times Honeycutt's total and benefits from outside spending on her side. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot.\n\nPolling is sparse and sponsor-skewed: a Republican-affiliated poll in early October showed Honeycutt up six, while Democratic-affiliated polls showed a one-to-six-point race. Most expert raters call the seat Lean or Likely Republican, though The Economist rates it a Tossup and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a three-in-ten chance. The race leans Republican, with genuine room for Lacore to close the gap on healthcare and affordability themes.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2812, "margin": -3.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2869, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3426, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2761, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3368, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2774, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2992, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2787, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3431, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3379, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2427, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2624, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2319, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2563, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2